  "confidence": "high",
  "narrative": "The combination of strong IP-driven demand, a rising baseline of 1B performances, and supportive 2026 growth signals makes a billion-dollar film by May 2026 plausible. Downside risks are real but are outweighed by the magnitude and frequency of 1B outcomes in recent years, justifying a high-confidence estimate around the 70% range.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.40,
      "basis": "Reference class: historical frequency of at least one film crossing $1B worldwide within a similar 12–16 month window surrounding May 1, 2026, given trending IP strength and expanding global markets. The anchor reflects a cautious baseline prior to simulating the explicit factor updates."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "IP strength and cross-franchise momentum",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Multiple high-profile IPs (e.g., Lilo & Stitch, Zootopia 2, Avatar: Fire and Ash) have demonstrated a high propensity to reach or exceed $1B, signaling a durable, escalating baseline for 2026."
      },
      {
        "factor": "China market dynamics and policy risk",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Policy shifts and import restrictions in China remain a meaningful source of downside risk that could dampen some 1B potential, especially for titles heavily reliant on that market."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Premium formats and rising ticket prices",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Higher average ticket prices and premium formats lift per-title revenue, increasing the likelihood that a tentpole reaches or exceeds $1B in global grosses."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Market volatility from strikes and slate crowding",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Labor strikes and crowded slates can suppress total box office year-to-date totals and limit the number of potential 1B titles, introducing headwinds."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Upcoming high-profile IP releases (e.g., Mario Galaxy Movie)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "New tentpole IP releases in 2026 tend to attract global audiences, improving the chance of a 1B film as interest in IP-led blockbusters remains strong."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Non-English language and international market strength",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Growing international demand, including non-English language blockbusters, broadens the global path to 1B beyond the US/China axis."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "The synthesis weighs IP momentum and international demand as the dominant drivers, with upside amplified by premium formats and continued growth forecasts. China policy and market volatility supply meaningful downside checks. The calibrated central probability (~0.72) reflects this balance, recognizing substantial upside potential from multiple gestating 1B titles while cautioning against asymmetrical risks in a few key markets."
